# Invite links route through the invite-preview function, which injects
# PER-TABLE OG tags ("ElleBell's Table · 2/4 seated") into the static
# invite page — and always answers 200 (crawlers refuse to card a 404).
# These are REWRITES: the browser URL keeps /join/CODE, so the page's
# pathname-parsing JS still reads the code — and the functions read
# kind + code from that same preserved pathname (parsePreviewRequest).
# GOTCHA: do NOT put ?kind=&code= in a destination here — Netlify
# silently DISCARDS destination query params (only the client's own
# query string is forwarded), which shipped every share as the generic
# brand card until 2026-08-10.
# /og/* serves the per-table card PNG (falls back to /assets/og-card.png
# for unknown codes). Every other unknown path still falls through to
# 404.html with a 404.
#
# /daily-deal/DATE is a shared Daily Deal result. It needs no function:
# the card a message app draws is the same for every date, so the page is
# a static file and only its JS reads the date from the preserved path.
# It answers 200 for ANY date on purpose — a crawler refuses to card a
# 404, and the app, not this site, knows which deals exist.
/join/*      /.netlify/functions/invite-preview   200
/invite/*    /.netlify/functions/invite-preview   200
/og/join/*   /.netlify/functions/og-image         200
/og/invite/* /.netlify/functions/og-image         200
/daily-deal/*  /daily-deal/index.html              200
#
# /receipt/<moment>?… is a shared GAME — a win, a loss, a wall game — as a
# printed receipt. receipt-preview injects its OG tags (and og:video, the
# card as a video, when the moment has a clip) into the static receipt page; the query
# string is the client's own, so it survives the rewrite.
# /og/receipt/<moment>.png?… renders the card for that same query, and
# /og/receipt-video/<moment>.mp4?… the same card as a short video with the
# moment's clip composed live in its header (og:video — Messages plays it).
/receipt/*           /.netlify/functions/receipt-preview   200
/og/receipt/*        /.netlify/functions/og-receipt        200
/og/receipt-video/*  /.netlify/functions/og-receipt-video  200
# /og/receipt-print/<moment>.mp4?… is the same receipt PRINTING — the slip fed up
# out of the app's printer — as a 9:16 video to post (Reels, TikTok, Stories).
/og/receipt-print/*  /.netlify/functions/og-receipt-print  200
#
# /code/CODE is a PROMO CODE (a teacher's; app migration 0113) — the page
# shows the code and where to enter it; code-preview injects the gift's
# card ("A rare joker is waiting") for real codes. /og/code/CODE.png
# renders that card. It IS in the app-links file: with the app installed
# the link opens the app's /code route, which redeems on open; this page
# is for everyone else (and its "Open it" link carries the code by scheme).
/code/*        /.netlify/functions/code-preview     200
/og/code/*     /.netlify/functions/og-code          200
